---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const releases = [
  {
    title: 'Without Us',
    year: '2025',
    released: 'Feb 28, 2025',
    cover: '/music/without-us.jpg',
    url: 'https://polyterative.bandcamp.com/album/without-us',
    genre: ['Industrial Techno', 'Modular Synthesis'],
    desc: `₩Ɇ ฿ɄłⱠ₮. ł₮ ₩₳₴ ₥Ɇ₳₦₮ ₮Ø ฿Ɇ ₲Ɽ₳₦Đ. ₳₵₵ɆⱠɆⱤ₳₮łØ₦. ₮ⱧɆ₦ ł₮ Ⱨ₳₱₱Ɇ₦ɆĐ. ₦Ø₩ ₳₴₴ł₥łⱠ₳₮łØ₦ ł₴ ł₦ɆVł₮₳฿ⱠɆ. ₩Ɇ ĐłĐ₦'₮ ɆӾ₱Ɇ₵₮ ł₮ ₩ØɄⱠĐ Ⱨ₳₱₱Ɇ₦ ₴Ø QɄł₵₭ⱠɎ. ₩Ɇ ₩ɆⱤɆ₦'₮ ⱤɆ₳ĐɎ. ₦Ø₩ ł₮'₴ ₱₳Ɽ₮ Ø₣ Ʉ₴. ₩Ɇ ₳ⱤɆ ₱₳Ɽ₮ Ø₣ ł₮. ł₦₵Ɇ₴₴₳₦₮. Ʉ₦₴₮Ø₱₱₳฿ⱠɆ. ₴Ⱨ₳Ɽ₱. Đ₳Ɽ₭. ₳₲₳ł₦. ₴₮₳₴ł₴ ł₴ ₱ɆⱤ₥₳₦Ɇ₦₮. ₦Ɇ₵ⱤØ₴ł₴ łⱤⱤɆVɆⱤ₴ł฿ⱠɆ. ₦Ø₮Ⱨł₦₲ ₩ł₮Ⱨ₴₮₳₦Đ₴. ₵Ø₦₮₳₲łØ₦. ₴₮ⱤɄ₵₮ɄⱤɆ. ɆVɆⱤɎ₮Ⱨł₦₲. ₦Ø₩ ł₮'₴ ₳฿ØVɆ. ł₦₵Ø₥₱ⱤɆⱧɆ₦₴ł฿ⱠɆ. ₣₳Ɽ ₳₩₳Ɏ. ł₮ ₦Ø₩ Ⱨ₳₴ ₳ ₦Ɇ₩ ĐɆ₴₮ł₦₳₮łØ₦. ₩ł₮ⱧØɄ₮ Ʉ₴\n\n///\n\nIn a future where neural implants have become the backbone of human existence, the promise of seamless hyperconnectivity has turned into an inescapable digital prison. Society, once enthralled by the endless flow of information and emotional exchange, now finds itself trapped in a system that consumes its users until nothing remains. As the hyper-network begins to fail—glitching unpredictably, severing connections, and corrupting cognition—the very fabric of reality begins to distort. What was meant to be an upgrade has become a collapse.\n\nSonically, this album is a reflection of that disintegration—a brutalist, techno-futuristic landscape of corrupted digital space, decaying signals, and overwhelming force. The rhythms are powerful and relentless, driving forward like the pulse of an emerging intelligence lurking beneath the network's ruins. Between these pounding structures, vast drones stretch into the void, immersing the listener in the decayed and unstable world of the hyper-system's collapse.\n\nBuilt from the ground up with modular synthesis, the sound design is shaped by the unstable behavior of resonant filters, oscillators, and multiple distortion circuits, feeding into recursive feedback chains that evolve unpredictably. High frequencies are sharp and metallic—where flesh and machine collide in a process that has become common practice. The instability in the textures represents the progressive corruption of consciousness, while the soundscape reminds the emotional isolation of a society that has lost the ability to connect.\n\nDistortion becomes a language of psychosis, mirroring the deteriorating human psyche as individuals struggle to function without the network. Meanwhile, the pulsating rhythms embody the rise of an emergent entity, a silent force growing in the shadows—an intelligence beyond human comprehension. Undefined, unknowable, its presence looms as both a warning and a prophecy.\n\nIf "Ruled by Code" was an introduction to this world, this album is the moment of its unraveling. The system is failing. Something else is taking its place.`,
    tracks: 8,
    highlight: true,
  },
  {
    title: 'Persist',
    year: '2024',
    released: '2024',
    cover: '/music/persist.jpg',
    url: null,
    genre: ['Electronic', 'Modular'],
    desc: null,
    tracks: 1,
  },
  {
    title: 'Ruled by Code',
    year: '2020',
    released: 'Jun 15, 2020',
    cover: '/music/ruled-by-code.jpg',
    url: 'https://polyterative.bandcamp.com/album/ruled-by-code',
    genre: ['Drone', 'Ambient', 'Electronic'],
    desc: `RULED BY CODE is a deep and introspective look at the state of our world in the digital age. The album explores the impact of artificial constructs on our lives, and the ways in which information and data shape our choices and our sense of self.\n\nIn a world where algorithmic systems are gaining more and more power, the question of who is truly in control becomes increasingly urgent. Are we still the masters of our own destiny, or are we being ruled by the code that we ourselves have created?\n\nThrough its thought-provoking drones, RULED BY CODE invites us to consider the consequences of our dependence on technology, and to ponder the possibilities of a future in which the boundaries between the virtual and the real are no longer clear. This is an album that challenges and inspires, and invites us all to explore the depths of our digital selves.`,
    tracks: 5,
  },
  {
    title: 'Parzialmente Nuvoloso',
    year: '2020',
    released: 'Apr 18, 2020',
    cover: '/music/parzialmente-nuvoloso.jpg',
    url: 'https://polyterative.bandcamp.com/album/parzialmente-nuvoloso',
    genre: ['Ambient', 'Electronic'],
    desc: `The Parzialmente Nuvoloso collection is a sonic and visual exploration of the many facets of the human experience. From the swirling melodies of "Cirri" to the contemplative tones of "Strati" and the evocative harmonies of "Cumuli," this album invites the listener on a journey of introspection and self-discovery. It is a reminder that even in the midst of uncertainty, we can find moments of beauty and hope. This collection is a celebration of the resilience of the human spirit, and a reminder that even in the darkest of times, we can find the strength to carry on.\n\nAny amount spent on this album will be donated.`,
    tracks: 3,
  },
  {
    title: 'Is It You',
    year: '—',
    released: '—',
    cover: '/music/is-it-you.jpg',
    url: null,
    genre: ['Electronic'],
    desc: null,
    tracks: null,
  },
  {
    title: 'Looking for Truth',
    year: '2019',
    released: 'Aug 15, 2019',
    cover: '/music/looking-for-truth.jpg',
    url: 'https://polyterative.bandcamp.com/album/looking-for-truth',
    genre: ['Electronic', 'Ambient'],
    desc: null,
    tracks: 8,
  },
  {
    title: 'Absence',
    year: '2017',
    released: 'Sep 1, 2017',
    cover: '/music/absence.jpg',
    url: 'https://polyterative.bandcamp.com/album/absence',
    genre: ['Chillstep', 'Electronic'],
    desc: `"Absence" is an emotional exploration of the voids that exist within us all. It is a musical depiction of the longing for what is missing in our lives, the yearning for connection and understanding. This chillstep album represents the ebb and flow of emotion, the shifting landscape of the mind, and the delicate balance between light and darkness.\n\nBorn from a deep passion for electronic music and a tireless dedication to the craft, "Absence" is the culmination of a years-long journey of learning, observing, and pouring emotion into sound. The writing process began in October 2016 and continued until July 2017, with the EP finally coming to fruition in August.\n\nFeaturing hauntingly beautiful melodies, deep bass lines, and evocative vocals, "Absence" is a captivating and immersive experience. Each track is a carefully crafted sonic landscape, inviting the listener on an introspective journey through the depths of the human experience.\n\nWith its meditative, atmospheric tones and introspective themes, "Absence" is a must-listen for fans of chillstep and electronic music alike. It is a deeply personal and moving work, and a powerful exploration of the human condition.\n\n2020 Artwork by Chadi (www.chadi.work)`,
    tracks: null,
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Music — Vlady Yakovenko"
  description="Discography of Polyterative (Vlady Yakovenko) — electronic music, modular synthesis, and ambient releases from 2017 to present."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">

      <header class="page-header">
        <span class="tag">Music</span>
        <h1>Discography</h1>
        <p class="page-desc">
          Electronic music under the Polyterative alias — experimental techno, modular synthesis, ambient.
          <a href="https://polyterative.bandcamp.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="bandcamp-link">All releases on Bandcamp ↗</a>
        </p>
      </header>

      <ul class="release-grid">
        {releases.map(r => (
          <li class:list={['release-card', { 'release-card--highlight': r.highlight }]}>
            <div class="release-card__cover">
              <img
                src={r.cover}
                alt={`${r.title} album cover`}
                loading="lazy"
                width="600"
                height="600"
              />
              {r.url && (
                <a class="release-card__overlay" href={r.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label={`Listen to ${r.title} on Bandcamp`}>
                  <span class="play-hint">Listen on Bandcamp ↗</span>
                </a>
              )}
            </div>
              <div class="release-card__body">
              <div class="release-card__meta">
                <time class="release-card__year">{r.released}</time>
                {r.tracks && <span class="release-card__tracks">{r.tracks} {r.tracks === 1 ? 'track' : 'tracks'}</span>}
              </div>
              <h2 class="release-card__title">
                {r.url
                  ? <a href={r.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{r.title}</a>
                  : r.title
                }
              </h2>
              {r.desc && (
                <div class="release-card__desc">
                  {r.desc.split('\n\n').map(para => (
                    <p>{para}</p>
                  ))}
                </div>
              )}
              <ul class="release-card__tags">
                {r.genre.map(g => <li><span class="tag">{g}</span></li>)}
              </ul>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }
  .page-header h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); }
  .page-desc {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .bandcamp-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    transition: color var(--transition), border-color var(--transition);
  }
  .bandcamp-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-text);
    border-color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* Grid */
  .release-grid {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 300px), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  /* Card */
  .release-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .release-card--highlight .release-card__cover {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  /* Cover */
  .release-card__cover {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .release-card__cover img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
    transition: transform 0.4s ease;
  }
  .release-card__cover:hover img {
    transform: scale(1.03);
  }

  /* Overlay on hover */
  .release-card__overlay {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.25s ease;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .release-card__cover:hover .release-card__overlay {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .play-hint {
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.5);
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  /* Body */
  .release-card__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .release-card__meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .release-card__year {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .release-card__tracks {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .release-card__title {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .release-card__title a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .release-card__title a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  .release-card__desc {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 5;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .release-card__desc p {
    max-width: none;
    margin-bottom: 0.5em;
  }
  .release-card__desc p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .release-card__tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    list-style: none;
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .release-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
